# Per-machine and per-person, never shared. `settings.json` beside it is the workspace's
# settings and is tracked; this one is whatever the person at this desk allowed today, and
# committing it would apply one machine's answers to everybody else's.
#
# This is the whole reason the two files have different names. Claude Code reads both and
# merges them, local winning, so the split is already the tool's -- it is only the tracking
# decision that is ours.
settings.local.json

.DS_Store
__pycache__/

# Runtime lock, written by the scheduler while a session is live. Machine-local and
# transient -- tracking it would commit one desk's in-flight state to everybody.
scheduled_tasks.lock

# The working agreements arrive here as `linkfile` entries from the goal manifest,
# pointing at `request-for-discussion/CLAUDE.md`. They are symlinks `repo` creates and
# removes, not content this repository tracks, and without these lines they show up as
# untracked files in every `repo status` forever.
#
# Claude Code reads a project CLAUDE.md from `./CLAUDE.md` OR `./.claude/CLAUDE.md`, which
# is why the link can live here at all. `AGENTS.md` is a different case: Claude Code does
# not read it, and the agents that do read it look at the repository root.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
